.213.0:5002.213.11"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?Classical]" target="latin:/?Classical"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#5660.235.0:5675.235.15"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?ProofIrrelevance]" target="latin:/?ProofIrrelevance"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#5755.240.0:5777.240.22"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?PL]" target="latin:/?PL"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#5840.245.0:5848.245.8"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?PLND]" target="latin:/?PLND"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#5871.249.0:5881.249.10"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?AlternativeNegationAndFalsityND]" target="latin:/?AlternativeNegationAndFalsityND"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#6143.260.0:6180.260.37"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#6537.272.0:6682.273.40"/></metadata>Conjunction where the second conjunct's well-formedness may depend on the truth of the first conjunct
   Curry-Howard analogue of Sigma types</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?DependentConjunction]" target="latin:/?DependentConjunction"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#6684.274.0:6710.274.26"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?DependentConjunctionND]" target="latin:/?DependentConjunctionND"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#6788.279.0:6816.279.28"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#7035.286.0:7262.287.120"/></metadata>Disjunction where the second disjunct's well-formedness may depend on the falsity of the first disjunct
   Curry-Howard analogue of an unusual union type where the second argument is only considered if the first one is empty</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?DependentDisjunction]" target="latin:/?DependentDisjunction"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#7265.288.0:7291.288.26"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?DependentDisjunctionND]" target="latin:/?DependentDisjunctionND"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#7375.293.0:7403.293.28"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#7636.300.0:7767.301.37"/></metadata>Implication where the implicate's well-formedness may depend on the truth of the implicant
   Curry-Howard analogue of Pi types</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?DependentImplication]" target="latin:/?DependentImplication"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#7769.302.0:7795.302.26"/></metadata></mref><mref name="[latin:/?DependentImplicationND]" target="latin:/?DependentImplicationND"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/logic/pl.mmt#7873.307.0:7901.307.28"/></metadata></mref></omdoc>